CORE
main.sh

^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[assertion\.1\] file main.sh line 3 assertion "\$\{#\}" -ge 0: SUCCESS$
^\[assertion\.2\] file main.sh line 4 assertion "\$\{#\}" -ge 2: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
shift 2 with fewer than two parameters makes dash exit, as for errors of
special builtins (XCU 2.8.1); the script continues only with $# >= 2
before the shift, so $# >= 0 after it, but not $# >= 2.
